# Welcome to your pod

This is your space on the web. What you keep here is yours: apps come to it,
and they ask you before they read or write anything.

## What is here already

- **`profile/card`**: your WebID, the address that says who you are
  ({{webId}}). It is public on purpose, so apps and people can check who they
  are dealing with. It says only what you put in it.
- **This README**, public too, so anyone who opens your pod's address knows
  what it is.
- **The list of what sits at the top of your pod** can be seen by anyone who
  has its address: the names only, not what is inside.

Everything you add is private: only you can open it, until you share it.

## Sharing, on your terms

Open an app that looks after your pod, choose a file or a folder, and say who
may see it. You can change your mind at any time, and taking access back works
at once. The apps that work with this server are listed on its home page,
[{{oidcIssuer}}]({{oidcIssuer}}).

## Apps and agents

- **An app you sign in to** acts as you: it can read and write what you can,
  for as long as its sign-in lasts (an hour, or up to a day if you let it stay
  signed in). The page where you say yes names the app first.
- **An agent** (an AI assistant, a script) has its own identity in this pod,
  under `profile/`. It reaches only what you share with it, and you remove it
  from the app you made it with.

## Your account

Your pods, your WebIDs and your password: [your account]({{oidcIssuer}}.account/).

